db.sqlite3
# Real production/legacy DB dumps used for the one-off historical-data
# restore work (see CLAUDE.md's "Restoring historical..." sections) sit
# untracked at the repo root, several GB each - Docker sends the whole
# build context to the daemon before applying this file's exclusions, so
# leaving these in blew that up to ~25GB and made every `docker build`
# glacial. None of them are needed to build the image.
*.sql
# Keep migrations/__init__.py (needed for Django to recognize these as
# migrations-tracked apps) - only the generated 0*.py files are excluded,
# matching .gitignore. makemigrations creates them fresh on every build.
*/migrations/0*.py
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern here only matches at the build context
# root - it needs the **/ prefix to actually match at any depth.
**/*~
.git
Dockerfile
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/__pycache__
.Python
env
